WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.800
So the Paw Patrol, they should totally be dead.

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:04.200
In the newest movie, part of a meteor hits Adventure City,

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.300
destroying the Paw Patrol tower before crashing down into the streets.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.500
Thankfully, the pups saved the day by clearing everyone into nearby buildings,

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:15.300
and in the final couple of seconds, hiding themselves behind things like newspaper stands and in the trunks of cars.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.800
But nah, that ain't doing anything.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.400
In reality, Adventure City would have been leveled.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:25.700
See, meteors move fast, between 11 and 77 kilometers a second, about 25,000 miles an hour.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:30.000
And because they have so much velocity, they are carrying a lot of energy, no matter how big they are.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.200
In 2013, for instance, a 19-meter meteor exploded over Russia with 30 times as much energy as the atomic bomb.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:41.200
Given the size of what you're seeing here in the movie, sorry, Paw Patrol, you're not just playing dead after that one.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:51.400
Hello, Internet! Welcome to Film Theory, the show that refuses to let sleeping dogs lie.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.900
So, did you guys wait in line to pre-order your tickets to the latest Paw Patrol movie like I did?

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:59.700
Because let me tell you, in our family, this was the most hyped movie ever in my life.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:03.600
Hold my pup pack, Avengers Endgame, the Paw Patrol Mighty Movie is where it's at.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:06.600
Now, you might be thinking I'm over-exaggerating, but no, this is actually a true story.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.400
This was my son Ollie's first official movie in a theater.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.700
Based on the fact that he shouted,

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.300
"This movie is so awesome!"

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:17.000
unprompted four times throughout the film, I'd say that it exceeded his expectations.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:22.400
Anyway, in case you don't know, Paw Patrol is a series about a group of rescue service puppies led by a boy genius named Ryder.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:27.400
Now, in our previous series, we uncovered the dark truth hidden under this polished, merchandise-friendly exterior,

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:34.300
exposing the fact that Ryder is actually a cutthroat capitalist using stray pups as cheap, expendable labor to do dangerous rescue missions,

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:37.900
paying them in cheap dog biscuits while he rakes in the government contracts.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:41.900
But one thing we've yet to touch on is just the basic logistics of this world.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:45.800
I mean, forget dogs acting as police officers and firefighters, these dogs can talk.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.200
Like, talk like normal humans.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.800
And while I've largely ignored that fact till now, since animated show gonna animate,

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:55.300
the new movie threw that fact into stark focus with this one scene right here.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:58.900
Oh my goodness! I can talk! I have so much to say!

00:01:58.900 --> 00:01:59.500
Meow!

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.600
Dogs are really the only creatures that can talk in this franchise.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.900
Every time a new pup gets introduced, bam, they can speak.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:08.000
They're action figure ready and your kid just found his new favorite character.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.800
You've got Everest way up in the mountains, Tracker deep in the jungles,

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.800
Sweetie and Claw over in Barkingsburg,

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:15.100
Liberty and the other dogs in the pound of Adventure City,

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.895
Rubble's family in Builder Cove.

00:02:16.895 --> 00:02:20.000
Basically, regardless of what breed they are or where in the world they are,

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.100
all dogs go to grammar school.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.919
But every other animal? No.

00:02:23.919 --> 00:02:27.549
We see owls, chickens, fish, cows, goats, bears, even cats.

00:02:27.549 --> 00:02:29.007
None of them are able to talk.

00:02:29.007 --> 00:02:31.600
Not a single word crosses their lips beyond what you'd expect.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.600
A hoot, a cluck, a moo here and there.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.100
Not even a syllable from the Kitten Catastrophe crew,

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.665
the animal sidekicks of the show's main villain.

00:02:38.665 --> 00:02:42.400
I mean, if any other animal were gonna talk in this franchise, you'd think it'd be them, right?

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.700
And yet, they're silent.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:48.100
Until this new movie comes out and suddenly they're given the power to speak through a magic space crystal.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.909
So, what's going on here?

00:02:49.909 --> 00:02:51.400
How do we explain that?

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.719
Well, I can do it in a single word for you: aliens.

00:02:53.719 --> 00:02:57.800
It's because the dogs in Paw Patrol aren't dogs, they're aliens.

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:01.400
And yeah, for all of you keeping track at home, this is the one where I officially lose my mind.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:05.800
Now, for the sake of completeness, I should probably mention a few exceptions to the only dogs talk rule.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:08.000
First, there are the mer-pups of Puplantis,

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:13.000
Puppy-fish hybrids who can't talk underwater, but can after they're magically altered into land-pups.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.200
What's going on?

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.000
Hey! I can speak!

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.900
Actual top-sider words!

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.100
I'm a land-pup!

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:23.200
This makes sense to me because the merpups presumably evolved from talking land puppies

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:28.500
and just lost the ability to speak once underwater since, you know, underwater speech ain't the most effective way to communicate.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:31.200
Also, can we just acknowledge my personal brain rot here?

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:35.500
I just said, this makes sense to me in regards to underwater mermaid dogs talking.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:37.700
Phew, that is a big self-revelation moment.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:40.200
Secondly, there's Wildcat and the Cat Pack,

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:44.300
a group of feline friends introduced in later seasons to help Ryder and the gang in some of the rescues.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:49.500
And again, this is called out as weird to the show's characters because cats in this world do not talk.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:51.400
What? You can talk?

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.600
You can talk? Of course I can talk.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:56.300
And yet no one bats an eye to the talking puppies.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.500
Why? What exactly is going on here?

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:01.800
Well, I think it all has to start with that clip from the Mighty movie that I showed off earlier,

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:06.700
where we watch as a member of the villain's kitten catastrophe crew gains the ability to speak through a space meteor.

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:08.600
Oh my goodness! I can talk!

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.200
I have so much to say!

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:13.200
The same meteor that gives the Paw Patrol their superpowers as the Mighty Pups

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:16.900
also gives other normal animals like cats the ability to talk.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.800
That right there seemed like an important detail to me.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.600
So, like the good boy that I am, I started to do some digging.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.300
And it seemed like someone was willing to throw me a bone.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:27.300
See, cats and dogs are actually very well equipped for full-on speech.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.800
They have a lot of the necessary organs required for the job.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:32.500
Vocal cords, vocal tract, even a voice box.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:36.300
This is how you see those cute videos of dogs and cats sounding like they're talking to their owners.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.400
I'm ready! Well hi!

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:42.400
What's holding back man's best friend and our feline familiars is actually their brains.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:45.100
They just lack a more sophisticated brain that would allow for speech.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:48.400
For us humans, the parts of the brain that help us to talk would be the Broca's area,

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:51.400
located in the left hemisphere, which enables speech and articulation,

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:55.000
and Wernicke's area, located in the posterior superior temporal lobe,

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.200
which helps you comprehend the written and spoken word.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:01.000
So, what does this space rock do into the cat that also gives it the ability to speak?

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:06.900
And how can it also be given pups that are already able to speak other superpowers like flight and super speed?

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:08.400
One word: radiation.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.800
Now, we've talked about this a lot before, specifically in our Magic School Bus theory,

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:14.300
but there's a lot of radiation out in space,

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:16.800
enough so that it could be deadly if you're not prepared for it.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.800
Extended time spent in space and the resulting exposure to radiation

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:22.400
can cause dramatic changes to an astronaut's behavior,

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:24.800
potentially even altering their DNA with mutations.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:28.800
And keep in mind that meteors are just bathed in radiation all day every day

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:31.000
for potentially hundreds of millions of years.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:34.700
Most of the time, this doesn't really result in any sort of long-term changes to the space rocks.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:39.100
In fact, most meteorites that fall to Earth aren't any more radioactive than boring old Earth rocks.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.100
But, there are plenty of exceptions.

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:44.400
In 2022, it was reported that a special type of radioactive meteorite,

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.100
known as a carbonaceous chondrite,

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:49.300
might have been what actually seeded life onto Earth to begin with.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:52.700
It's feasible that what's going on here is that this meteorite that we see in the Paw Patrol

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:55.100
is one of these carbonaceous chondrite meteors,

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:57.700
falling to Earth and mutating these dogs and cats.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:05:59.700
It's actually something even called out in the movie.

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:03.400
There are normal meteors, but this one right here, this is one of the special ones.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:08.500
It is actively called out as one of the few meteors floating around in space that has special powers.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:10.000
So, there you have it, right?

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.000
We know that space radiation can mutate people and alter their behavior,

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.700
we know that meteors can be bathed in space radiation,

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:19.900
and we know that in this world, irradiated meteors are able to give creatures the ability to talk.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:22.100
So, what's that all have to do with the Paw Patrol?

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:24.900
Animals that were able to talk before any meteors?

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:28.700
Well, I suspect that all the dogs in the Paw Patrol-verse aren't dogs at all.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.500
I think they're aliens.

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:32.200
Now, before you say anything, I get it.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.900
That sounds like a big ol' leap.

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:35.200
And normally, I'd agree.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:39.600
But in this show, aliens are a well-established and frequently utilized part of the lore.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:43.400
A pair of aliens, a mother and her child, are recurring characters across the series.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.000
And while these two look like your typical aliens,

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:48.300
there's also this completely separate species of alien space rocks.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:49.300
But even that's not all.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.100
The space alien has a doll based on

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:52.900
a relic from the rhombozoid galaxy,

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:56.100
implying that there's yet another species floating around out there.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:59.600
All in all, this proves that aliens come in many different shapes and sizes here.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:03.500
So puppy-shaped aliens evolved by the radiation of space to speak?

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:04.800
It's not out of the question.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:08.900
And what's more, seems like these aliens have a really keen interest in Adventure Bay,

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.600
and specifically with the Paw Patrol.

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:12.500
They're spotted multiple times throughout the series,

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:14.900
sometimes just flying overhead on the outskirts of town,

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:17.500
or studying the local wildlife outside of Adventure Bay,

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:21.800
but also occasionally stopping by to play a literal game of Frisbee with Ryder and the boys.

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:25.800
It kinda makes you wonder if the aliens are watching Adventure Bay specifically.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:29.500
We also see them taking an active interest in dogs with superpowers.

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:31.500
In the episode, Pups Save Floating Friends,

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:34.400
we see the aliens pulling up a video of Apollo the Superdog.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.700
A few years later, and boom!

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:39.200
An alien space meteor gives our faithful pups their superpowers.

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:40.000
Coincidence?

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.200
Eh, maybe.

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:45.700
All in all, I suspect that the dogs in the Paw Patrol universe started as a race of aliens,

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:49.600
able to communicate due to the mutations that space radiation had on their system.

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:54.100
At some point, representatives of the species crashed down onto Earth and spread across the planet,

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:57.300
diversifying and breaking out into the different breeds that we see today.

00:07:57.400 --> 00:08:00.400
Some went on to become mer-pups, losing the ability to speak underwater,

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:03.200
while others tried mating with native animals, the cats,

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:07.600
yielding the small minority of largely non-viable genetic anomalies like the cat pack.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:10.500
But at this point, thousands, even millions of years later,

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:14.200
humanity just accepts talking dogs as a fact of life not worth mentioning.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:17.900
It's just part of how dogs, as created, operate within this world.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:19.900
Except someone here knows the truth.

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:22.500
Someone knows that dogs are more than meets the eye,

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:24.300
and that someone is Ryder.

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:26.900
I suspect that he knows all of this, because, let me tell ya,

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:30.300
Ryder's reaction to all this alien stuff is incredibly strange,

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:34.300
strange enough that I started getting suspicious of our evil little capitalist mastermind.

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:36.900
See, despite everything that he's seen and done throughout his life,

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:40.800
Ryder is still skeptical of a lot of what the Paw Patrol encounters across their adventures.

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:43.500
For instance, he really doesn't believe in ghosts,

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.500
just straight-up dismissing them without a second thought.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:46.300
Ghosts aren't real!

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:48.700
He's even hesitant to believe any stories about the mer-pups,

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:51.400
despite having encountered other mythical creatures before.

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:54.400
Well, nobody's ever gotten a real good picture of a mer-pup.

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:55.900
It could've been something else.

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:59.100
But do you know what Ryder's reaction is to hearing that aliens are around?

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.900
It's not shock, it's not dismissal, it's not even skepticism.

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:05.100
I found a melon that was actually an alien, and he zapped me with this cool bubble thing,

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:06.300
and I floated in the air like,

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:07.100
Whoa!

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.700
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:10.100
Where's the alien now?

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:12.300
Yeah, Ryder immediately skips past the whole,

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:13.700
Are you sure it was an alien thing?

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:14.900
And just jumps straight into,

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:15.700
Well, where was it?

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:18.100
There's no hesitation in his voice, no doubt.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:20.500
It's almost like he already knew that aliens were a thing,

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:22.900
and he was just waiting for them to come around Adventure Bay.

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:27.300
And this is important because it's not like everyone else in the series just knows that aliens are real.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:30.500
Mayor Goodway is shocked the first time that aliens visit the town.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:31.700
There you are!

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:32.900
Ahhh meep!

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:33.700
Oh, dear.

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:35.700
This is not an everyday occurrence,

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:38.300
and Ryder is not acting normally here.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.500
Then I noticed something else.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.100
All the technology that Ryder makes,

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:42.500
and all that he has up in the Lookout,

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:46.100
sure does look a lot like the technology that's present in the alien spaceship,

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:49.100
enough so that the space alien recognizes the Lookout just at a glance,

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:52.100
and heads inside when his spaceship crash-lands in Adventure Bay.

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:53.100
And I totally get it.

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:54.100
When you put them side-by-side,

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:58.500
the only difference between the spaceship's interior and the Lookout is the color of the paneling,

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:00.100
enough so that you kind of have to ask:

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.700
Is this the same technology?

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.300
Even Ryder in the show says this,

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:05.900
The Lookout looks so much like a spaceship,

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:07.700
he's trying to fly it home.

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:09.700
There is definitely a connection here.

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:13.500
And listen, I know that this is just a cartoon for children about talking dogs reusing assets,

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:16.100
but there are just too many coincidences in this world.

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:18.700
Not only does the alien recognize what to do with the Lookout,

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:22.300
but Ryder is able to use the alien's tech without any sort of trial and error,

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:25.700
instantly figuring out how to open the container holding the space rock alien.

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:28.300
Additionally, Ryder's tech, it doesn't just look like the alien tech,

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:31.100
it is instantly compatible with it on more than one occasion.

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:35.300
The space alien's mother is able to hijack the Lookout's communication system with zero effort.

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:39.300
And Ryder's just able to tap into the alien communication system by putting his pup pad into

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:40.700
Super Long Distance Mode!

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:42.500
and it immediately picks up their signal,

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:45.100
almost as if it were specifically designed to be able to do that.

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:46.300
Even without technology,

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:48.700
when they weren't able to make radio contact with the aliens,

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:50.900
Ryder knows exactly how to get their attention,

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:53.700
making a crop circle to signal to them from space.

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:55.900
I mean, the only conclusion that we can take from all this

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:58.900
is that Ryder is somehow in cahoots with these aliens, right?

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:00.700
Or at the very least, that he's aware of them.

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:01.900
And there's a good reason for that.

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:05.300
You see, not only are the Paw Patrol and all these dogs aliens,

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:07.100
Ryder, Ryder is an alien too,

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:09.700
and not only are the Paw Patrol and Ryder aliens,

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:13.100
but every human that you see in this series is also an alien.

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:15.500
Aliens, aliens everywhere, aliens!

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:18.100
Seriously, have you ever noticed that all the humans in this world

00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:20.700
have only three fingers and one thumb on their hands?

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:24.100
The fact that this is so consistent tells me that this isn't some weird regional thing

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:25.900
or a quirk of the people living in Adventure Bay.

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:29.100
No, this is a consistent trait across their entire species.

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:30.700
And that's when it clicked for me.

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:32.100
They're all aliens.

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:35.100
And the thing that proves that the humans in this world are also aliens?

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:36.300
In the Mighty Pups special,

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.900
we see a shot of the Paw Patrol planet from orbit.

